# NOTICE

## What this package is, and is not

`atomfind` locates atoms in an ALREADY-RECONSTRUCTED three-dimensional phase volume. It is a
downstream consumer of ptychographic reconstruction output and contains no reconstruction
code. In particular it contains **no part of the cSAXS PtychoShelves MATLAB package**, and is
therefore not a derivative work of it. This package is released under the MIT License (see
LICENSE).

## Upstream software used to produce the input data

The reconstructions this package analyses were produced with the **cSAXS ptychography MATLAB
package** (PtychoShelves), developed by the Science IT and the Coherent X-ray Scattering (CXS)
groups, Paul Scherrer Institut, Switzerland, which is distributed under its own academic,
non-commercial licence. That licence governs the reconstruction step, not this package. Any
publication describing reconstructions made with it must state:

> Data processing was carried out using the cSAXS ptychography MATLAB package developed by the
> Science IT and the coherent X-ray scattering (CXS) groups, Paul Scherrer Institut,
> Switzerland.

and cite the relevant PtychoShelves / difference-map references.

The forward simulations that generated the 4D-STEM data used **abTEM** (Madsen and Susi, Open
Research Europe 1, 24 (2021)).

## Data

The reference structure `PTO6_STO6_18_18_labyrinthPoscar.vasp` is a relaxed PbTiO3/SrTiO3
supercell **provided by collaborators** and used with their agreement. It is redistributed here
for reproduction of the published result. Please contact the authors before reusing it for an
unrelated purpose.
